In its first quarterly meeting of 2026, the People’s Bank of China (PBOC) pledged to maintain a “flexible and efficient” monetary stance to support the nation’s 4.5%–5% growth target. The central bank will provide financing/credit support on major infrastructure and public services while navigating heightened global uncertainty fueled by the U.S.-Israel-Iran conflict.



