The S&P Global UK Manufacturing PMI was revised down to 51.0 in March, dropping from February's 51.7 and missing the preliminary estimate of 51.4. While the sector remained in expansion territory for the third consecutive month, production volumes fell for the first time since September 2025 as geopolitical uncertainty and the Middle East conflict weighed on growth expectations

Euro area preliminary annual CPI is estimated to have jumped to 2.5% in March, up from 1.9% in February and slightly below the 2.6% consensus. This "energy shock" marked the first annual increase in energy costs in nearly a year, largely driven by escalating Middle East conflict. Conversely, core inflation (excluding energy, food, alcohol, and tobacco) continued to moderate, falling to 2.3% from 2.4% in the previous month

